        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Civil rights movement</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">The southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, above all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alabama">Alabama</a>, Mississippi, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arkansas">Arkansas</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a> and the Carolinas, with campaigns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/washington-dc">Washington, D.C.</a>, and in northern cities such as Chicago</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1954–1968: from the Supreme Court’s ruling in Brown v. Board of Education to the assassination of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther-king-jr">Martin Luther King Jr.</a> and the Fair Housing Act; its roots reach back to the 1930s and 1940s</span></div>
